      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We start by applying the logarithm power rule:\n$\\log_b (a^n) = n \\cdot \\log_b a.$\nSo, the cotangent of the right angle of the triangle can be calculated as:\n$\\cot \\theta = \\frac{\\log_4 27}{\\log_4 9} = \\log_9 27 = \\log_9 3^3 = \\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nNext, we find the sine of the tangent using the Pythagorean trigonometric identity:\n$\\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 \\theta = 1.$\nSubstituting into this equation, we get:\n$\\sin^2 \\theta + \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2 = 1.$\nSimplifying further:\n$\\sin^2 \\theta + \\frac{9}{4} = 1.$\n$\\sin^2 \\theta = \\frac{1}{4}.$\n$\\sin \\theta = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}.$",
